      "page_title": "What Hooks Are & useState Basics",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What A Hook Is",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Plain function whose name starts with `use`",
            "Lets a function component tap React features",
            "State, lifecycle, context — between render calls",
            "A component is a function re-run top-to-bottom",
            "Hooks give that function a memory that survives"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Life Before 16.8"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Stateful logic lived only in class components",
            "Reuse needed HOCs and render props",
            "Result: wrapper hell in the component tree",
            "Constructors, binds, `this` boilerplate"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Class split one concern across 3 lifecycles",
            "didMount / didUpdate / willUnmount",
            "Unrelated concerns merged into one method",
            "Hooks group by concern: one sub, one useEffect"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Ship & Compatibility"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Landed in React 16.8, Feb 2019",
            "100% backward compatible — no class rewrite",
            "Classes and hooks coexist in one app",
            "Opt-in per component; migrate one at a time"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. The Core Seven"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Hook",
            "Gives you"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "useState",
              "one state slice"
            ],
            [
              "useReducer",
              "many-action state"
            ],
            [
              "useEffect",
              "outside-world sync"
            ],
            [
              "useContext",
              "context value"
            ],
            [
              "useMemo / useCallback / useRef",
              "cache / cache fn / box"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Not For Classes",
          "items": [
            "Hooks do not run in class components",
            "`this` is irrelevant in hook code",
            "Biggest trip-up when porting a class"
          ],
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "jsx",
          "lines": [
            "const c = new AbortController()",
            "fetch(url, { signal: c.signal })",
            "return () => c.abort()  // cancels in flight"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "jsx",
          "lines": [
            "useEffect(() => {",
            "  window.addEventListener('resize', onR)",
            "  return () =>",
            "    window.removeEventListener('resize', onR)",
            "}, [onR])  // same ref required to remove"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Four Lines, No Class"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "jsx",
          "lines": [
            "function Counter(){",
            "  const [n,setN] = useState(0)  // memory",
            "  const up = () => setN(n+1)",
            "  return <button onClick={up}>{n}</button>",
            "}"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. useState, The Shape"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "jsx",
          "lines": [
            "const [n, setN] = useState(0)",
            "// [value, setter] — array by convention",
            "const [rows] = useState(() => parse(csv))",
            "// lazy: parse runs once, not per render"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Initial value used ONLY on the first render",
            "Later renders ignore the argument entirely",
            "Setter identity is stable — safe to omit from deps"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "The Parens Are The Bug",
          "text": "`useState(heavy())` calls heavy every render and throws the result away. `useState(heavy)` defers it to mount."
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`n` is a const captured by this render",
            "The setter schedules; it never assigns",
            "State is per instance: two Counters, two counts"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "State Updates, Batching & Immutability",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. A Request, Not An Assignment",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "jsx",
          "lines": [
            "const [n, setN] = useState(0)",
            "function bump(){",
            "  setN(n + 1)",
            "  console.log(n)   // 0 — the OLD value",
            "}"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Bail-Out & Slices"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Same value by `Object.is` lets React bail out",
            "It then skips re-rendering that subtree",
            "Many small slices beat one big object",
            "`const [age,setAge]=useState(0)` per field"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Functional Updater"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "jsx",
          "lines": [
            "setN(n + 1); setN(n + 1)   // +1 total",
            "setN(p => p + 1)",
            "setN(p => p + 1)           // +2 total"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`p` is the latest queued value, not the closure",
            "Use it when next state derives from previous",
            "Also inside async callbacks, timers, effects"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Batching & The Update Queue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Each setter pushes an update onto a queue",
            "At render React replays the queue over base state",
            "Many setters in one handler: one render, one paint"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Fired from",
            "React 17",
            "React 18"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "React event",
              "batched",
              "batched"
            ],
            [
              "setTimeout",
              "no",
              "batched"
            ],
            [
              "promise .then",
              "no",
              "batched"
            ],
            [
              "native listener",
              "no",
              "batched"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. flushSync Escape Hatch"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "jsx",
          "lines": [
            "import { flushSync } from 'react-dom'",
            "flushSync(() => setN(1))  // sync re-render",
            "el.scrollTop = el.scrollHeight  // read now"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Immutability"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "jsx",
          "lines": [
            "state.items.push(x)",
            "setItems(state.items)    // same ref, no render",
            "setItems(i => [...i, x]) // new ref, renders",
            "setUser(u => ({...u, age: u.age + 1}))"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Spread is shallow — nested needs nesting",
            "`setS(s => ({...s, addr:{...s.addr, city}}))`",
            "Derived values do not belong in state",
            "Compute `const total = items.reduce(...)` in render"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. A List On The Fiber",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Each fiber holds a singly-linked list of hooks",
            "Stored on the fiber's `memoizedState` field",
            "Each node: memoized value, queue, next pointer",
            "Values live on the fiber, not in the closure"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "render starts",
              "i = 0",
              "call reads hooks[i]",
              "i++",
              "next hook"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Call Order: The Hook List Inside",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Identity Is Call Order"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "No key, no name — position is the identity",
            "Mount: append one node per hook call",
            "Update: walk the same list, node N for call N",
            "A conditional hook shifts every later index"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Toy Model"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "let hooks = [], i = 0",
            "const useState = init => {",
            "  const j = i++          // position = id",
            "  hooks[j] ??= init      // first render only",
            "  return [hooks[j], set(j)] }"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Mount vs Update"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Phase",
            "List op",
            "Value from"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "mount",
              "append node",
              "initial arg"
            ],
            [
              "update",
              "walk node N",
              "queue replay"
            ],
            [
              "outside render",
              "none",
              "throws"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. A Shifted Index"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "array",
          "spec": {
            "cells": [
              "n: 0",
              "name: ''",
              "effect"
            ],
            "indices": true,
            "pointers": [
              {
                "index": 0,
                "label": "useState('') lands here",
                "ink": "red"
              }
            ],
            "highlight": [
              0
            ],
            "dim": [],
            "caption": "skip call 0 → every later hook reads the wrong slot"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`name` now reads `n`'s stored value",
            "The effect reads `name`'s node",
            "React throws ==Rendered fewer hooks than expected=="
          ],
          "style": "cross"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Inside A Hook Node"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Field",
            "Holds"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "memoizedState",
              "current value"
            ],
            [
              "baseState",
              "value before queue"
            ],
            [
              "queue",
              "pending updates"
            ],
            [
              "next",
              "following hook"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. Stale Closure, Live"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "jsx",
          "lines": [
            "const [msg, setMsg] = useState('')",
            "const send = () => setTimeout(",
            "  () => alert(msg), 3000)",
            "// alerts msg as of the CLICK render"
          ],
          "note": "later typing never reaches this closure"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Ask: Which Render?",
          "text": "When a value looks stale, find the render whose closure created the callback. That render's consts are what it sees."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "8. Why State Survives"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Local variables are recreated on every call",
            "State is read back from the fiber by ==position==",
            "Setters enqueue; React **re-runs** the function",
            "Unmount drops the fiber — and its hook list"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Toy Model Limits",
          "items": [
            "Real list lives per fiber, not global",
            "Setters queue updates, not assign",
            "`Object.is` bail-out skips renders"
          ],
          "ink": "purple"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "The Rules of Hooks & Fixing Breaks",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. New Closures Every Render"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Each render: new props, new consts, new functions",
            "Old closures still exist and still see old values",
            "Stale closure = render #1's callback firing at #10",
            "Local variables die; fiber state does not"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Dispatcher Swap",
          "items": [
            "React swaps hook impl: mount vs update",
            "Outside a render there is no dispatcher",
            "That is how 'Invalid hook call' is thrown"
          ],
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. The Two Rules"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "1. Call hooks only at the top level",
            "Never in conditionals, loops, nested fns, after return",
            "2. Call only from components or custom hooks",
            "Not from utilities or class methods"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Why, In One Snippet"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "jsx",
          "lines": [
            "if (isLoggedIn) {",
            "  const [n] = useState(0)  // index shifts",
            "}",
            "const [m] = useState('')   // wrong slot"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Positional Identity Is The Reason",
          "text": "A skipped or extra call misaligns every later hook on that component. The rules are not style — they are the storage model."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Hoist The Hook, Branch The Value",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "jsx",
          "lines": [
            "const [x, setX] = useState(0)  // always runs",
            "const shown = isLoggedIn ? x : null"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "The condition moves into the value, not the call",
            "`if (!data) return <Spinner/>` sits below all hooks",
            "Loops: never `items.map(() => useState())`",
            "Extract a child so each item owns an instance"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. The Early-Return Trap"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "jsx",
          "lines": [
            "function List({ data }){",
            "  if (!data) return <Spin/> // ✗",
            "  const [q, setQ] = useState('')",
            "  // data arrives: one MORE hook",
            "}"
          ],
          "note": "move every hook above the return"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. One Hook Per Item"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "jsx",
          "lines": [
            "items.map(it =>",
            "  <Row key={it.id} item={it} />)",
            "function Row({ item }){",
            "  const [open, setOpen] =",
            "    useState(false)  // own slot",
            "}"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Runtime Tells",
          "items": [
            "'Rendered fewer hooks than expected'",
            "'Rendered more hooks than during the previous render'",
            "Both = a call count changed between renders"
          ],
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Hook inside `if`, `&&`, or ternary",
            "Hook inside `.map`, `for`, or a callback",
            "Hook after an early `return`",
            "Hook in a plain `formatX()` helper"
          ],
          "style": "cross"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Lint Signals & Meeting useEffect",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Custom Hooks Are Exempt"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A `useX` may call hooks — it inlines into the caller",
            "Rule 2 bans plain utilities, not custom hooks",
            "The `use` prefix is how eslint picks targets"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Lint & Runtime Signals"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Signal",
            "Meaning"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "rules-of-hooks (error)",
              "order violation"
            ],
            [
              "exhaustive-deps (warn)",
              "missing reactive dep"
            ],
            [
              "'Invalid hook call'",
              "broken rules"
            ],
            [
              "same error",
              "React vs ReactDOM mismatch"
            ],
            [
              "same error",
              "two Reacts installed"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "The One Exception",
          "items": [
            "React 19's `use()` may be called conditionally",
            "It reads a promise or context mid-branch",
            "Every other hook still obeys rule 1"
          ],
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. useEffect: Signature & Timing"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`useEffect(setup, deps?)`",
            "Setup runs after commit, after the browser paints",
            "For syncing with systems outside React",
            "Requests, subscriptions, timers, DOM, logging, widgets"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Not A Lifecycle Callback",
          "text": "Ask what external thing must stay in sync with this render — not when does this fire."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. The Return Contract"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Return nothing, or return a cleanup function",
            "Anything else is an error",
            "So `useEffect(async () => {})` is illegal",
            "An async fn returns a Promise, not a cleanup"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "jsx",
          "lines": [
            "useEffect(() => {",
            "  const run = async () => setD(await get(id))",
            "  run()",
            "}, [id])"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. useLayoutEffect"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Runs sync after DOM mutation, BEFORE paint",
            "Only to measure layout or kill a visible flicker",
            "It blocks painting — default to useEffect"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. Effect Or Not?"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Effect fits",
            "Not an effect"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "subscribe to a store",
              "derive render data"
            ],
            [
              "fetch for visible id",
              "handle a click"
            ],
            [
              "start a timer",
              "copy props to state"
            ],
            [
              "drive a non-React widget",
              "chain state updates"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "8. Measure Before Paint"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "jsx",
          "lines": [
            "useLayoutEffect(() => {",
            "  const h = ref.current",
            "    .getBoundingClientRect().height",
            "  setTipH(h)  // re-render pre-paint",
            "}, [])"
          ],
          "note": "user never sees the wrong position"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Sync `document.title` with state",
            "Open a chat connection for `roomId`",
            "Log a page view when the page shows"
          ],
          "style": "check"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Effect Order & The Dependency Array",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "useEffect: after paint, non-blocking",
            "useLayoutEffect: before paint, blocking",
            "StrictMode dev: mount, unmount, remount once",
            "That double run never happens in production"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Order Per Commit",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "DOM updated",
              "layout effects (sync)",
              "browser paints",
              "useEffect flushes"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. What Never Belongs In One"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Transforming data for render — compute in render",
            "Handling a user event — put it in the handler",
            "Setting state the effect also depends on = loop",
            "Effects run per committed render, so it never ends"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "jsx",
          "lines": [
            "useEffect(() => setFull(a+' '+b), [a,b])",
            "// costs a second render for nothing",
            "const full = a + ' ' + b  // just compute it"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Three Dep Forms"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Deps",
            "Runs"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "omitted",
              "after every render"
            ],
            [
              "[]",
              "once after mount"
            ],
            [
              "[a, b]",
              "mount + when a or b changed"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. How Deps Compare"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`Object.is` per slot, positionally",
            "Not deep equality — twin objects differ",
            "Array length must be constant between renders",
            "Else: 'final argument changed size between renders'"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. The Correctness Rule"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "List every reactive value read inside the effect",
            "Props, state, context, and values derived from them",
            "`exhaustive-deps` is correctness, not style",
            "Disabling it is how stale-closure bugs ship"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Unstable Identities"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Objects, arrays, functions in the body: new each render",
            "Listing them re-runs the effect every render"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Rank",
            "Fix for an unstable dep"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "1",
              "move the value inside the effect"
            ],
            [
              "2",
              "hoist outside component if constant"
            ],
            [
              "3",
              "depend on `user.id`, not `user`"
            ],
            [
              "4",
              "useMemo / useCallback, last resort"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. Primitive Deps Win"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "jsx",
          "lines": [
            "useEffect(() => {",
            "  load(user.id)",
            "}, [user.id])  // not [user]"
          ],
          "note": "new user object, same id: no re-run"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Strings and numbers compare by ==value==",
            "Parent re-creating `user` no longer re-syncs",
            "Read only the fields the effect needs"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Stale Deps & The Cleanup Contract",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Already Stable",
          "items": [
            "State setters — omit freely",
            "Refs and `ref.current`",
            "`dispatch` from useReducer"
          ],
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Empty Deps Is A Claim",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`[]` claims the effect never needs to re-sync",
            "If it reads a prop, that claim is a lie",
            "The prop stays frozen at its mount value"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. The Frozen Interval"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "jsx",
          "lines": [
            "useEffect(() => {",
            "  const id = setInterval(() =>",
            "    setCount(count + 1), 1000)  // stuck at 1",
            "  return () => clearInterval(id)",
            "}, [])  // fix: setCount(c => c + 1)"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Churn & The Compiler"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A dep that changes too often is a design signal",
            "Move to `useReducer`, depend on stable `dispatch`",
            "React Compiler (19+) auto-memoizes",
            "Dep rules themselves are unchanged"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Cleanup Contract"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "The returned function is the cleanup",
            "Runs before the next run of that same effect",
            "And once at unmount",
            "Dep change: cleanup(OLD) first, then setup(NEW)",
            "It closes over its own render — no bookkeeping"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Must-Clean List"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "setInterval / setTimeout",
            "addEventListener",
            "WebSocket, EventSource, store subscriptions",
            "Intersection/ResizeObserver, animation frames"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "jsx",
          "lines": [
            "useEffect(() => {",
            "  const id = setInterval(tick, 1000)",
            "  return () => clearInterval(id)",
            "}, [])"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Fetch Races"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Two fast requests can resolve out of order",
            "The slow older one overwrites with stale data",
            "Cleanup on `[url]` is the fix point"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. Cleanup Timeline"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Event",
            "React runs"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "mount (id=a)",
              "setup(a)"
            ],
            [
              "id a → b",
              "cleanup(a), setup(b)"
            ],
            [
              "id b → c",
              "cleanup(b), setup(c)"
            ],
            [
              "unmount",
              "cleanup(c)"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 1
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "jsx",
          "lines": [
            "useEffect(() => {",
            "  const id =",
            "    requestAnimationFrame(draw)",
            "  return () =>",
            "    cancelAnimationFrame(id)",
            "}, [])"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Cleanup Mirrors Setup",
          "text": "Every subscribe gets an unsubscribe, every add a remove, every open a close. Read the setup, write its inverse."
        }
      ]
    },
